text = "[b][u]The Files: How Important are they ?[/u][/b]"

[node name="Label1" type="Label" parent="Left/MarginContainer/Nodes" parent_id_path=PackedInt32Array(1644936578) index="2" unique_id=435658224]
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(1, 0)
layout_mode = 2
text = "At work, you have two best friends: not me, your manual (I think you know why), and the files.

Unfortunately, as the safe so kindly asked us, your manual doesn’t contain all the information needed to get the secret code.
In its mind, it probably thought the secret code was too easy to crack (if you think that’s stupid or pointless, I completely disagree with you).

How do these wonderful and very useful files work?
It’s very simple; they install on your computer in two ways:
- The “no consent respect Microslop like behavoir” where the files are downloaded to your device without your consent
- The “exemplary good behavior,” where the system asks you if you want to download the file, and to which location.
It is strongly encouraged to download them, as they may contain information necessary to help you find the secret code"
autowrap_mode = 3

[node name="Label1" type="Label" parent="Right/MarginContainer/Nodes" parent_id_path=PackedInt32Array(1257509253) index="2" unique_id=229044363]
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(1, 0)
layout_mode = 2
text = "I think you have all the information you need; the following pages are clearer and easier to understand than the one you looked at.

Good luck, and don't screw it up.


- Diego"
